Agriculture has been an important sector for Cambodians since the birth of this territory. Cambodians all over the country are engaged in agriculture. Takeo, the capital of Nokor Kork Thlok, is a land with great potential for agriculture, and the province ranks third in agriculture after Prey Veng and Battambang.
According to Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Takeo is also a province with a total population of 1,014,473, of which 518,880 are women, with 79% of the population completely dependent on agriculture. Farming, fishing and raising animals to support their livelihood.
According to the Minister, Takeo Province has 264,000 hectares of land for agricultural production, including 180,000 hectares of wet season rice, 8,000 hectares of dry season rice and 4,000 hectares of plantation land.
For the early rainy season rice harvest so far, 20,015 hectares have been achieved, equivalent to 38.19% of the total land area in the province, with an average yield of 4.66 tons per hectare and yield. 93,879 tons. According to the estimated food balance in 2020, Takeo province has 525,764 tons of rice left, equivalent to 821,507 tons of rice, an increase of 22,004 tons more than last year, which can be sold to domestic and foreign markets.
