The workshop is under the Higher Education Improvement Project (HEIP), funded by the World Bank. The workshop has three main objectives:
1: Study the general employment rate of students after graduating from university 2: Study the employment rate of students in accordance with the skills that students study 3: Study the salary and type of work of students after graduation Studies.
In addition, the workshop aims to strengthen institutional capacity and build the capacity of management and administrative officers to develop guidelines on post-graduation student studies.
This workshop will support the University of Battambang in developing a system of postgraduate study for the production of an official study report.
The University of Battambang will submit the report of the study results to the Board of Directors of the University of Battambang and disseminate it to the public through the social media and the official website of the University of Battambang. The report of the results of this study will help improve the curriculum of the University of Battambang with quality to meet the needs of society and the national and international labor market.
In this workshop, the Rector would like to express his deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia, the World Bank, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, especially Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Mr. York Ngoy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Director. Higher Education Improvement Project (HEIP) and Mr. Mak Ngoy, Director General of the General Department of Higher Education and Chairman of the Higher Education Improvement Project.
