DC-Cam will name its library "Samdech Mey Library"
(Phnom Penh): Dedicated to the highest reverence to Samdech Mey, the Queen Mother of the Khmer Nation in support of the study, research and promotion of the history, culture and contemporary art of Cambodia. Education, education and culture are essential to the identity and development of a nation and the progress of humanity.
DC-Cam strives to ensure that Cambodia's history and art, both ancient and contemporary, are preserved, protected and open to the general public. Recently, Ambassador Dr. Holio Jeldres, former Personal Secretary and biographer of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, donated his entire collection, including books and other documents, to the Center Library. Cambodian documents.
In recognition of this invaluable contribution, as well as the highest homage to the lifelong efforts of Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk to Cambodia, the Documentation Center of Cambodia will be named Its library is called "Samdech Mey Library" with the permission of the Queen Mother.
In addition to the collections of the Ambassador Dr. Holly Jelloz, the Samdech Mey Library contains historical documents, books and other materials on genocide and human rights in Cambodia. DC-Cam is continuing to expand its collection.
The library will be an important resource for students and general researchers, serving as an open institution to the public to increase awareness of Cambodia's history, culture and contemporary art.
