(Phnom Penh): Negotiations on the establishment of a free trade agreement between Cambodia and China were officially closed on July 20, 2020, after opening negotiations for half a year.
The closing ceremony of the Free Trade Agreement between the two countries was held today via video, with the Cambodian side represented by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, and the Chinese side represented by Mr. Zhong Shan, Minister of Commerce of the People's Republic of China
At the closing ceremony of the talks on the establishment of a free trade agreement, the two trade ministers praised the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, an agreement that reflects the traditional long-term relationship as well as Cooperation in a comprehensive partnership between the two countries.
The two trade ministers noted that the successful completion of negotiations on a free trade agreement in a short period of time shows the willingness of the two countries' leaders to strengthen closer ties and Extensive.
He added that the free trade agreement will bring many economic and social benefits to the people of the two countries through the liberalization of trade in goods and services, the promotion of comprehensive investment, as well as cooperation in a number of areas. Well.
Following the announcement of the closing of negotiations on the agreement, the next step will be for the two sides to implement their respective internal procedures leading to the signing of a bilateral free trade agreement in 2020.
Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang at a bilateral meeting on January 20-23, 2019 in Beijing, decided to study the possibility of establishing a Cambodia-China bilateral free trade agreement. Expand trade, investment, services and cooperation to achieve a total trade target of 10 billion US dollars by 2023.
If the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China is signed, it will be the first free trade agreement for Cambodia. The Ministry of Commerce claims that based on the joint principles agreed by the negotiating team, if the two governments agree on the text of the proposed agreement and market opening, Cambodia's export growth is expected to increase. Up about 20 percent.
At the same time, the growth of foreign investment is also expected to increase significantly, which is a source of income and jobs for Cambodians.
