Court charges the owner and manager of a chemical coffee factory that authorities raided in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province
The accused, who are represented by the prosecution, are: First, Thon Nath, female, 33 years old, currently residing in Trapeang Kteah village, Kraing Makak commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, Occupation: Owner of Lingkae and Bean handicrafts (bail) and second: Name: Luot Leang, Male, 24 years old, Present Residence: Trapeang Khtom Village, Kraing Makak Commune, Ang Snoul District, Kandal Province.
Defendants Thon Nath and Luot Leang have already roasted coffee and beans mixed with illegal chemicals and sold them on the Cambodian market, which poses a high health risk in their handicrafts. Accused to buy from Orussey Market once a month per month and then sell on the market per kilogram for 20,000 to 30,000 riels.
When sold to the market per kilogram, the price is 20,000 to 30,000 riels per day, sold from 50 kilograms to 70 kilograms, and the defendant also made a confession that the coffee processing. Packing and marketing is unlicensed.
After the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor's Office examined the facts, legal facts, evidence and confessions of the two defendants, the Provincial Prosecutor's Office issued a concluding order to send the case to the Trial Chamber No. 398 dated 16 May. July 2020:
* First, the accused Thon Nath, a 33-year-old female, and Lot Leang, a 24-year-old male, were charged with counterfeiting products (roasted coffee and beans containing chemicals) at the location of the roasted coffee and bean brand. Thon Nath was located in Trapeang Khmum village, Kraing Makak commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province on July 2, 2020 in accordance with the provisions of Article 17, Article 63 and Article 65 of the Law on Quality and Safety Management of Products and Services.
* Second: To send the criminal case No. 1183, dated July 08, 2020, of the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor's Office to the Kandal Provincial Court for trial in accordance with the law.
In this operation, the inter-ministerial authority of the CPPCC found that the location of the coffee and bean roasting handicraft site had many errors: no branding, no product registration, no quality control certificate. , On the coffee packaging does not have the address and how to use, on the coffee packaging contains 100% pure coffee, in which the packaging mixes many ingredients and unhygienic location.
In addition to the above exhibits, the police did not confiscate or damage any items, and the prosecutor allowed the joint police to close the location and invite the owner of the above location to clarify the relevant case at the Secretariat of the CPPCC. To follow the procedure. Samdech Techo Hun Sen sent a message of condolence for the death of Pring Sakhorn.
