(Phnom Penh): "Phnom Khnong Phsar" resort has been becoming very popular with tourists, especially those who like to walk in the forest to visit the beautiful nature. Phnom Khnong Phsar is an area of "natural paradise" buried in a large mountain forest located in Tangpong village, Rolak Kang Cheung area, Ta Sal commune, Oral district, Kampong Speu province.
Arriving at the place that tourists want is on the mountain behind the market, they have to go through many obstacles and take about 4 to 5 hours. Difficult road conditions have become an obstacle for all these tourists, requiring them to walk. Although a little difficult, they still struggled to get fresh air in the mountains.
The Governor of Kampong Speu Province, Mr. Vy Samnang, acknowledged that it is difficult for tourists who want to enjoy the lush natural scenery of the "Phnom Khnong Phsar" resort. In a press conference on the morning of July 20, 2020, the spokesman of the Royal Government, Mr. Vy Samnang confirmed that the province is studying to make a suitable road for the convenience of tourists.
In addition to considering the road to travel, the governor of Kampong Speu also announced plans to build a bathroom or toilet to make it easier for tourists to use. So far, the resort of "Phnom Khnong Phsar" does not have a bathroom or toilet yet, which is also a concern for tourists who go to camp on it.
In addition, Mr. Vy Samnang is also committed to making this eco-tourism resort a beautiful and hygienic place through the use of toilets. The provincial governor also called on tourists to properly dispose of garbage.
(Phnom Penh): New colors, new logos and modern design, high efficiency, easy to use, a new presentation of the new look of all types of lubricants of TOTAL and ELF on the occasion of the opening The official inauguration of Total Station 100, Tuol Key Branch, located on National Road 3, Phnom Penh, this morning, July 20, 2020.
