The Royal Decree was issued on July 18, 2020 after the prostration of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and was promulgated on July 20, 2020.
Road in the middle of Koh Dach commune has been rehabilitated to facilitate people's travel
(Phnom Penh): A dirt road through the center of Sangkat Koh Dach, Khan Chroy Changvar at Otanong point connecting Wat Ampor Phal, Chong Koh village to Tuol Tanong, Koh Dach village has been rehabilitated to facilitate people's travel. .
The groundbreaking ceremony for this road was held on the morning of July 20, 2020 under the chairmanship of Mr. Nop Channarin, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection and Chairman of the Working Group for Sangkat Koh Dach, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh.
Mr. Nop Channarin said that this is a solution to the requests of local people raised in a public forum in November 2019.
He said that through public forums, the working group addressed to the people according to some requests, such as the installation of poles and light bulbs using solar energy on remote public roads, promoting the provision of timely public services, promoting the crackdown on drugs and cockfighting. Mobile was successful.
Mr. Nop Channarin continued that after conducting a public forum under the guidance of Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group to assist Phnom Penh, the Koh Dach Sangkat Assistance Team continued to monitor all requests. Blessings of the people without leaving and addressed step by step according to the possibility and size of the necessary needs. If some of the work is large, the working group has already sent the request to the Khan and Capital level.
Regarding the rehabilitation of this road, Mr. Pat El, Chief of Koh Dach Commune, said that according to the project, the rehabilitation work can be completed within two weeks.
Mr. Pat El said that this road is 10 meters wide and 800 meters long, implemented by five groups of companies to serve the people in the whole Koh Dach commune, which people have requested in the public forum.
The construction of this road has the support of Mr. Pat El, Sangkat Chief and Deputy Chief and Sangkat Council, who have worked hard to find philanthropists both inside and outside the locality to help until it can run as requested.
Please note that the Otanong Road, which has been open, the team has cleared and raised the land above the flood, making it easier for people to travel. Midea brand is an internationally recognized brand offering burial 100 days special price
(Phnom Penh): Midea has held a promotion program in the provinces for 100 days from the date of this announcement to thank all customers for their support, the company has a lot of discounts Unprecedented and fun games for all parents and siblings.
The promotion for the discount lasts up to 100 days from the date of this announcement, so please parents and siblings to join the promotion, do not miss this great program.
A Kampong Thom resident cried excitedly and won 50 million Riel from Cambodian beer can earrings
(Phnom Penh): Under the shade of mango in the middle of a rice field, at around 12 noon, Im Mey's family bought three cans of Cambodian beer for three people to enjoy with a farmer-style lunch.
Mr. Immy described it like this: "Just put your buttocks together immediately, I dig out the beer for a moment, look at the canned earrings, lest he have any prizes, then the surprising big prize is 50 million riel on the canned earrings, and I "I called my wife, who was sitting next to me, and she jumped out of bed and screamed for joy. I was so excited that I cried for her."
The 50 million riels will be used to buy a small plot of land to dig a fish pond and expand the business of raising chicken cages to earn extra income, because farming in recent years has always lost money.
Mr. Immy did not come to open the prize himself because he was busy with his farm, so his son Hong Sitola had already exchanged the prize with Khmer Breweries instead.
Drink Cambodian beer responsibly !!
Local traders in Kampong Ror, Svay Rieng province, bring tons of rice to sell in Vietnam every day, despite Kovid
(Svay Rieng): Despite the outbreak of Kovid-19, a group of traders exported about 250 tonnes of rice to Vietnam at the military canal near the Prey Vally international border crossing in Prey Vally village, Thmey commune, Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province. To 300 tons.
Mr. Thach Ratana, Director of Svay Rieng Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that rice will be exported to Vietnam for one month from June 16 to July 16, 2020. 5,150 tons of military canals near the Prey Vally international border gate.
Heng Samrin University Tbong Khmum Shows Success of 50 Plus 50 Curriculum in Cultivation and Breeding
(Tbong Khmum): Heng Samrin University Tbong Khmum organized a study visit to learn from the students' success in planting and breeding and raising animals for teachers from primary, secondary and high schools. In Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province, at Heng Samrin University, Tbong Khmum, in Sralop commune, Tbong Khmum district, on July 18-19, 2020.
The experience was directly led and presided over by Mr. Touch Visal Sok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, as well as Mr. Pin Vannaro, Rector of Heng Samrin University, Tbong Khmum and Mr. Sit Khon, Rector of Kamchay Mear University, Prey Veng Province.
Mr. Pin Vannaro stated that the strength that drives the success of Heng Samrin Tbong Khmum University in the short term is that the school focuses on quality, especially the program on theory 50% and practice 50% practical. All colleges, especially the Faculty of Agriculture, where students have already practiced successfully in the past on farming and animal husbandry.
Mr. Touch Visal Sok mentioned that the main purpose of leading teachers here is to exchange experiences, understand simple technical tips, but get high results.
He added that teachers also play an important role in outreach work because all knowledge is disseminated by teachers in schools and communities at low cost, especially fast and highly effective.
The Secretary of State also strongly hopes that after gaining this agricultural knowledge, teachers would like to bring the knowledge to disseminate to the villages, districts and schools, so that the people who have vacant land to cultivate and raise animals to Facilitate family life during Kovid-19 disease.
