(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, stated that as of July 20, 2020, the payment of cash subsidies to poor and vulnerable families during the anti-Kovid period 19 For the first round, 93% reached more than 530,000 families, a small number have not yet opened.
Addressing the press by Mr. Vong Soth during a workshop on the procedures and procedures for the implementation of cash assistance programs for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 to district governors prepared On July 20, 2020 at the Ministry of Social Affairs.
In addition, Minister Vong Soth said that the remaining people, please hurry to open before the deadline for the first round, which closes on July 24, 2020. For those who have already opened, please go to open the second round from July 25 to August 24, 2020, which is the second month of assistance from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
At the same time, Minister Vong Soth also said that in order for this implementation to be successful, transparent, accountable and to reduce the challenges to the maximum, the program steering committee, which is the operator of the implementation of this program, asked for continued cooperation. On the following activities:
* First, requesting the Royal Government's working group to visit the capital and provinces to continue to monitor and inspect the identification of the poor, both round and round, and to request the implementation of the meat subsidy program for poor and vulnerable families during Kovid 19.
* Second: Request the Board of Governors of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans to continue to encourage the Commune / Sangkat Administration to implement consistently in accordance with Prakas No. 166 S.A.Y. Prok dated 15 June 2020 on the implementation of the procedure. And the implementation of cash support programs for poor and vulnerable families
* Third: Request the Ministries, Institutions and all stakeholders, especially the sub-national administration, to continue to actively promote the cash subsidy program for poor and vulnerable families during the Kovid 19 period to the local people, especially the poor families. Equity cards are valid using the same broadcast system as the mechanisms used in the past to spread Kovid 19.
Please note that in order to receive this allowance, poor and vulnerable families must have a valid equity card based on poverty level: poor level 1 (poor) or poor level 2 (poor) and go to verify the program list. Donate cash to poor families during the fight against Kovid 19 at any commune hall.
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tay, Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian People's Party in Kampot Province, requested nearly 1,000 new members to be honest and diligent in maintaining good relations with the people and striving to maintain unity. Internally, enhance the capacity and virtue to fulfill the duties of the motherland.
Mr. Chiao Tai made this request on July 19, 2020, when he presided over the induction ceremony of 985 new members in political life with the Cambodian People's Party in Kampong Trach district, Kampot province. .
During the ceremony, Mr. Chiao Tai and many relevant party members welcomed the nearly 1,000 new members who have volunteered to participate in the party's political life and asked all new members to promote patriotic conscience, discipline and unity. Within the party, the party is loyal to the party, with each collective leader responsible for accompanying the Royal Government, local development and society.
He added that Cambodia has transformed from the killing field of the Pol Pot genocidal regime, from the battlefield of the chronic war, from the ashes to the land of peace, unity, stability, freedom, democracy, the rule of law and development in all areas, for all people. Live in harmony and hope under the roof of the same constitution and the cool shade of the King, the highest shrine.
