(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, instructed the Deputy Commissioner, Fire Prevention Office to increase the regular education to vulnerable workers such as gas stations, sales locations and Add gas, especially to other vulnerable areas, and they should have fire hoses ready to provide first aid in the event of a fire.
Lt. Gen. Thet made this instruction on the morning of July 20, 2020, on the occasion that he chaired a meeting to promote and conduct inspections at karaoke clubs to guide education and disseminate measures. Of the Ministry of Health and the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Hall to turn those places into restaurants to cooperate in preventing and controlling the spread of Kovid 19 virus.
The General Commissioner's instructions came after a massive fire at a gas station on Street 63, Sangkat Boeung Reang, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, on the evening of July 18, 2020, killing four people and injuring five others. Serious injuries.
On that occasion, the Deputy Commissioners, the 14 District Police Inspectors participated in the comments, provided reports, and made regular inspections at all karaoke club locations to make it clear that those clubs, if open, must be transformed into Restaurant in accordance with the instructions of Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
The commissioner gave a lot of advice to all district inspectors to set up regular checkpoints at all karaoke clubs to avoid theft, contrary to the instructions that could cause the spread of Kovid 19 virus.
As for drug cases, Lt. Gen. Thet said that although for some time now, the specialized office has investigated and cracked down on many cases and many places where drugs are used and traded. The commissioner stressed that this issue to the specialized offices and the 14 district police inspectorates to monitor and search for targets and locations that trade in both small and large scale.
