Training to become a real force that is absolutely loyal to the motherland, respects the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
On behalf of the General, Professor Chea Dara, all officers of the National Defense University, I would like to express my gratitude once again and wish Lt. Gen. Dr. Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Commander of the Army, good health and complete all tasks. Siem Reap Red Cross Branch Donates a House to Disabled Families in Daun Sva Village, Samrong Ya Commune, Puok District
(Siem Reap): Mrs. Teang Eng Tea Seiha, Vice Chairman of Siem Reap Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, and her colleagues on the afternoon of July 19, 2020, visited and handed over a humanitarian house initiated by Mr. Tea Seiha, Branch Committee Chairman. Siem Reap Red Cross and with the support of Mr. Tea Vichet and Mrs.
The humanitarian house was given to the family of 65-year-old Kiri (left leg paralyzed) and his wife Nhek Mon, 59, with nine family members living in Daun Sva village, Samrong Ya commune, Puok district, Siem Reap province. Nowadays, they work for a living and earn some income to support their families. This humanitarian house is 6 meters x 6 meters, has two rooms, a galvanized roof, tiles, smart walls, tiled floors, 0.4 meters high, built on his own land, size 9 meters x 14 meters.
Speaking on that occasion, Ms. Teang Eng Tea Seiha brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as Mr. Tea Seiha, Chairman of the Branch Committee, who always cares about the well-being of the people. Not everyone is of any caste, color, creed, religion or political affiliation, as the saying goes, "The Cambodian Red Cross is everywhere for everyone, leaving no one behind."
She also encouraged people to know how to grow mixed crops near their homes, and this is the rainy season, so be careful of thunderstorms and take care of your health, especially young children, if you find it uncomfortable, send them to the center immediately. The nearest health. She also instructed the community, all family members to know how to clean and maintain this new house to be a warm home forever.
Tycoon Tea Vichet also stated that he was very happy to see the achievements he had made through the Cambodian Red Cross and reached the hands of vulnerable and disadvantaged people, especially at home. Given now is pretty decent beyond his imagination.
Please note that in the handing over ceremony, humanitarian donations were also added, including: 2 mosquito nets, 2 blankets, 2 sarongs, 2 scarves, 2 mats, 60 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 2 fishing rods, 2 water tanks. , 10 T-shirts, some kitchen equipment, and a budget of 400,000 riels. For this family, Venerable Preah Preah, Honorary Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch, Puok District, donated some gifts and a budget of 100,000 Riels.
(Kampong Chhnang): Every Cambodian still remembers the genocidal regime, which was a killing field in a fake regime called Democratic Kampuchea, which ruled Cambodia from 1975 to early 1979. More than three million innocent Cambodians have been killed everywhere in Cambodia.
In particular, in a pagoda called Wat Samdech Mony, also known as Wat Samdech Chakto, in Khon Rang commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, which was used by Pol Pot as one of the largest genocidal crime centers in Kampong Chhnang province for torture and cutting. Killed nearly 20,000 innocent people, and the residents there, who are still alive today, will never forget this dark past.
Wat Samdech Mony, about 40 kilometers from Kampong Chhnang city, was used by the Pol Pot regime as a prison for torture and the most brutal killing of prisoners during the 3-year, 8-month, 20-day killing field regime.
According to village elders who lived near the pagoda and witnessed the torture of prisoners more than 40 years ago, the Pol Pot regime did not torture prisoners here. Unlike the torture in Tuol Sleng prison in Phnom Penh, such as interrogation by removing fingernails and toenails, hanging the feet up, immersing the head in a jar of water, placing handcuffs on the floor, and by Other atrocities.
After their interrogation was completed, they were taken to be killed more than 1 km from Wat Samdech Mony, where three large graves were already dug up. There, too.
Ta Chun Kem, 72, now the abbot of Wat Samdech Mony, said that in 1975 all the people were evacuated by the Pol Pot regime, with no one left in each village. This pagoda is also unoccupied.
In 1976, they used Wat Chakto and Wat Krous, which are located next to each other in Khon Rong commune, Boribo district, as the two pagodas. Serious prisoners and places of torture before the prisoners were taken out of here to be killed, and the prisoners here were also brought from all districts in Kampong Chhnang province In some provinces, come here as well.
According to those who know the history of Wat Samdech To, which was used by Pol Pot as a place to torture the above Cambodian people, said that the prisoners who were killed in Wat Samdech This table has about 20,000 people, according to the list of stamps where the Pol Pot regime recorded the names of all the prisoners they took to be imprisoned at this pagoda.
At present, Wat Samdech Chakto is considered by the Royal Government and the people of Kampong Chhnang province as a place to pay homage to the spirits of the dead in the Killing Fields regime every year, because in this pagoda, there are stupas to keep some of the dead and a large number of items. Both exhibits of torture at that time were kept at Wat Choeung Ek in Phnom Penh.
Everybody in Kampong Chhnang province knows this pagoda because it is our place of religious worship and a historical place where the genocidal people have left a heartbreaking tragedy. Khmer children of all generations can not forget.
A New House Donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to War Disabled Veterans in Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Som Sun, President of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province, on the afternoon of July 19, 2020, led his colleagues and local authorities to meet and hand over a new house as a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Director. Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association to the families of war veterans living in O'Romdeng village, Trapeang Russey commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Som Sun said that the new house to be handed over to the disabled veterans at this time is 4 meters x 6 meters, built of concrete pillars, steel bones, walls and roofs, galvanized iron, flooring, flooring, stairs, stairs to be handed over to Mr. Chreung. Nhanh, 58, and his wife, Duong Ream, 58, have four dependent children, for a total of six family members.
Mr. Som Sun also stated that the disabled veteran Chreung Nhanh joined the army in 1985 with the rank of lieutenant colonel in the 179th Division and was injured by a landmine on 13 February 1992. At the Battle of Svay Chek, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Mr. Som Sun also brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to greet the veterans and the people, who always take care of your well-being and life at all times and encouraged the veterans. And people strive to practice farming and animal husbandry to improve the livelihood of the family.
Mr. Som Sun also reminded the people and veterans to continue to be very careful to protect themselves and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease must be strictly implemented in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health in the world. He has infected more than 14 million people and left more than 600,000 dead without a cure.
It should be noted that during the handover ceremony, the working group of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province brought the donation of Lt. Gen. Dr. HUN Manet, including: 50 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 2 cans of fish sauce and soy sauce. Some budget as well.
