Mr. Vy Samnang pointed out that in 2019, the provincial administration received 92,654 million Riels, equivalent to 510% of the annual plan, with a budget of 75,043 million Riels, equivalent to 99% of the annual plan for provincial development. . The provincial governor showed the following progress:
* Land, Urban Planning and Construction: As of 2019, systematic land registration has been implemented in 515 villages in 32 communes of 8 districts. In total, from the date of implementation until December 2019, 408,938 plots were entered and 333,592 cards were distributed to the people.
Dispute Resolution and Mediation: In total, by 2019, the provincial administration had received 80 complaints or letters, 23 letters from the national level related to land issues, and 57 complaints from the people: resolved by the provincial administration. 27 cases, 31 cases are still being resolved, 6 cases have not been resolved yet and 16 cases have been sent to the municipal administration and relevant departments and units.
The implementation of the policy of 9 safe villages and communes and the results of the Kampong Speu Provincial Competition Movement have achieved better results than last year, with the results of the first category being 85 out of 87 communes, the second category has 2 communes, which Third, the commune has no ranking, no.
Commercial work: There are 10 potential commodities in the province, such as palm sugar, sugar cane, vegetables, chicken, pork, rice, mango, corn, construction sand and construction stone. There are 745 enterprises, of which 349 companies. 142 branches and 254 enterprises, 20 markets and 5 community markets.
* Industry, Science and Innovation: As of the beginning of July 2020, there are 161 large factories in Kampong Speu province, employing a total of 120,734 people, 98,684 women. Of these, 143 factories are operating and 18 factories are under construction. There are a total of 1,508 small and medium enterprises and handicrafts employing a total of 13,395 people, 6,281 of whom are women.
* Tourism: There are 13 tourist sites in Kampong Speu province, including 4 historical sites (including archeological caves, Phnom Chas archeology, Phnom Preah archeological site, Te Teuk Pou historical site and Phnom Kaek Pong temple resort).
There are 8 natural resorts, including Preah Suramarit Kosamak Kirirom National Park, Kirirom Recreation Center, Chambok Ecotourism Community, Chreav Ecotourism Community, Ampre Phnom Kirirom Phanh Resort, Golf Course, Rithy Kirisen Monorom Golf Resort and Norak Borey Museum. There are two adventure tourism sites: Phnom Oral and Phnom Khnong Phsar.
* Natural Resources and Environment: There are two national parks, Preah Suramarit-Kosamak National Park "Kirirom" and Bokor National Park with a total area of 22,073 hectares, of which Monivong Bokor National Park is 2,637 hectares and Preah Suramarit Kosamak National Park Kirirom 19,436 hectares.
Social work Veterans and youth rehabilitation: Kampong Speu province has 14 child care centers with 638 children, 273 females. There are 50 orphans living in the state center, 25 females. There were 1,383 people with disabilities who received physical rehabilitation services at the centers and 422 people received policies, subsidies and health care services.
