(Phnom Penh): Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and Samdech Thammavisut Vongsa, Sao Ty Heng Samrin, handed over 180,000 health masks to the Ministry of Health and Kantha Bopha Hospital for use and distribution to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
The handover ceremony was held on the morning of July 20, 2020 at the National Assembly building through Mr. Keo Piseth, Director of the Cabinet of the President of the National Assembly, as the High Representative of Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
During the ceremony, the Director of the Office of the President of the National Assembly expressed his appreciation for the sacrifices and efforts of the medical team and all relevant authorities who have sacrificed their physical and mental strength to perform their noble duties effectively and efficiently in this difficult time. High responsibility under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Mr. Keo Piseth said that the President of the National Assembly has always actively cooperated with the Royal Government in preventing the spread of Kovid 19, in which he always educated and instructed the people to follow the protection measures of the Ministry of Health and encouraged All members of the National Assembly regularly distribute alcohol masks or hand-washing gels and foodstuffs to the people.
The President of the National Assembly strongly believes that the mask given by Samdech to the Ministry of Health and Kantha Bopha Hospital on this occasion will be beneficial to the work to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease in Cambodia even more dangerous to the health of Cambodians. No more.
Through Mr. Keo Piseth, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin once again called on the people to continue to implement the protective measures that the Ministry of Health has set out, such as wearing a mask, washing hands and soap, to keep the safety gap. To infect Kovid 19 to your family and community.
