(Kandal): Residents of 3 communes of Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province, Chhwang commune, Chrey Las commune and Phnom Bat commune, along National Road 151, which has just been beautifully paved, now have received additional drainage system. Support of the Minister of Water Resources to avoid any flood congestion and prevent road damage.
Recently, Mr. Thorn Sovanna, Governor of Ponhea Leu District, led the youths to help install sewers along National Road 151 to release water from the road because this is the rainy season.
Mr. Thorn Sovanna said that seeing the difficulties of the people living along National Road 151 in the above location, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology and Chairman of the working group to help Ponhea Leu district and The team poured nearly 12 kilometers of DBST rubber.
After pouring the rubber, the Minister also inspected that this road, if there is no drainage system, the road will be damaged soon, and he also supported the drainage along this road, which is more than 12 kilometers long. Place on either side of the road.
Residents on both sides of National Road 151 were overjoyed and delighted to receive this beautiful road and drainage system and thanked Mr. Lim Keanhor and his team. Because this road used to be difficult to travel in the dry months, the soil is very dusty, the rainy months are muddy, it is difficult to travel and transport agricultural products.
The district governor added that not only are the people happy, but people are also involved and donated. Riga in front of his house to make the drainage was successful.
(Stung Treng): After receiving widespread publicity related to the law and safety policy of the village-commune, this morning, July 20, 2020, the people in Sesan district, Stung Treng province handed over 39 recycled weapons to be handed over. Let the authorities save it.
According to Colonel Pheap Leap, Sesan District Inspector, after two plans, the Provincial Unity Command as well as the Provincial Police Commission, the specialized force of the District Police Inspectorate, cooperated with the village-commune-administrative authorities of Sesan District. Disseminating weapons to the people is illegal.
Colonel Pheap Leap continued that after the awareness campaign, the people woke up and handed over weapons to the competent authorities at the 7 administrative police stations of the Sesan District Police Inspectorate.
Currently, the above 39 weapons of the National Explosive Ordnance Office of Stung Treng Provincial Police have been kept at Stung Treng Provincial Police for further procedures.
