Mr. Ly Sary, Deputy Governor, said that these 31 families do not know whether they are really poor or not, but these 31 families should not come to the province to ask for a poor card from that province because Claiming that the village chief, commune chief, commune chief are the eyes and noses of the province, doing something is really right.
Ms. Prum Sinath, Director of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Planning Department, said that on July 21, she will identify the 31 families. She recalled that the characteristics of obtaining a really poor card include people living alone, childless, homeless, living in poverty.
It should also be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has officially launched a program to provide cash to people living in poverty and vulnerable to the effects of Kovid-19 disease. To ensure that poor people who are experiencing real difficulties receive support from the Royal Government, work to update poor families and vulnerable people during this period.
