(Kampong Thom): Conflict between Kampong Thom Provincial Forestry Administration and the Tonle Sap North Inspectorate and people in the area of "Anlong Thmor" forest extension and rehabilitation station, Boeung Lvea commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province, until 22 firearms exploded last July 16, 2020 recently.
The cause of the explosion was that forestry administration officials accused residents of illegally occupying land in the "Anlong Thmor" forest extension and rehabilitation station area, while residents claimed that they Occupied this land for many years until it was cultivated as other crops.
Two villagers who were handcuffed by the Kampong Thom Provincial Forestry Administration and the Northern Tonle Sap Inspectorate confirmed that the Forestry Administration had accused them of obstructing the work of the authorities. In that incident, the villagers accused the forestry administration officials of using violence on them before pushing them into the car.
According to the villagers, the officer who beat him was Heng Try, a contracted officer of the Forestry Administration. Other residents who witnessed the incident asked each other to ask for the two, but the authorities did not allow and reached an argument with each other, while the forces shouted to the people, "Dare to enter, shoot one. "
At that time, more and more people came and heard the sound of two bullets exploding at about 4 pm. Hearing this, a group of people thought they had been shot and people came in. Suddenly, there was a series of 22 explosions.
Regarding this case, Mr. Bun Sothy, Director of Forestry Administration of Kampong Thom Province, told reporters that in this incident, one of his officers was injured when a group of people threw an ax while his officer was in the car.
He said that in the case of the explosion, his officers fired to disperse the people because the people came from the cashew plantation armed with knives and axes, but this incident did not injure any people. He asked all citizens to participate in the implementation of the law and to protest peacefully if there is any disagreement.
