(Phnom Penh): Some necessary measures have been put in place by the National Committee for Disaster Management to respond to the floods that may occur in the rainy season of 2020. The measure was unveiled at a disaster response planning meeting and the launch of the "PRISM" platform this weekend.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, said at the ceremony that disaster response planning as well as floods in the rainy season are necessary and care must be taken to avoid accidents. Serious on the people.
To prepare for the disaster as well as the floods, Senior Minister Kun Kim announced a number of necessary measures to be taken. Necessary measures to be taken include: early warning of impending floods, preparedness, means, means to rescue vulnerable people, minimizing risks and taking action. Restore after low tide.
Regarding the use of the "PRISM" system, the Senior Minister requested all relevant departments to review and provide additional suggestions on points that need to be improved to better meet the situation and the actual needs of the people. Local citizens.
