(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has decided to appoint 39 interns in the post of Deputy Judge of the Judiciary and assign them to work in 20 Capital-Provincial Courts.
The Royal Court, obtained by Fresh News on July 19, 2020, said that the 20 capital-provincial courts where the 39 judges will be working include: Kandal, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Battambang, Siem Reap, Oddar Meanchey, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Kampot. Kampong Speu, Takeo, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Pursat, Prey Veng, Kratie, Stung Treng, Koh Kong, Mondulkiri and Phnom Penh.
The Royal Decree, issued on July 18, 2020, states that the 39 judges are entitled to basic salaries and other allowances as required by law. The right to receive other allowances, the right to be promoted or promoted is calculated from May 08, 2020.
Please read the following Royal Decree: The strong wind hit the houses of 23 families in Chamkar Leu district, the Local Strengthening Committee and the district Red Cross inspected the situation and distributed gifts to the victims
(Kampong Cham): A gust of wind hit the houses of 23 families, causing the roofs of houses to open in Veal Thnong village, Prasor village and Daunthy village, Bos Khnour commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province. In fact, on the morning of July 19, 2020, the working group of the Cambodian People's Party and the district Red Cross sub-branch inspected the situation and distributed gifts to the families of the victims.
The ceremony was held under the guidance of Mr. HUN Manit, Member of the CPP Committee and Chairman of the Chamkar Leu District Assistance Team, and then Mr. Yon Duk and Mr. Nguon Vito, Deputy Chairman of the Bos Khnor Commune Assistance Team, represented Mr. Duong Udom, Team Leader. National work to help Bos Khnour commune and Mr. Khlot Chenda, Honorary President of District Red Cross Sub-Branch to distribute donations.
Speaking on that occasion, the working group of the Cambodian People's Party and the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch brought a message from the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to all victims. .
The working group stated that the leadership always pays attention to the well-being of the people at all times, no matter where, no matter where there are difficulties or accidents, there is always a CPP working group. Cambodians and the Red Cross always arrive without any racism or political affiliation.
At the same time, the team also advised people to be careful because this is the rainy season, so rain and wind can occur at any time, so be careful. In addition, be careful to protect yourself from Kovid-19 by washing your hands frequently with soap or alcohol and wearing a mask where necessary.
After the meeting with the people, the working group also continued to inspect the installation of 18 sewerage systems to release water and pour a 50-meter-long road across the stream to facilitate people to travel to the fields. Daun Thi village, Bos Khnour commune, Chamkar Leu district, with a budget of 6,320,000 Riels.
Crack down and burn more than 5,000 marijuana trees planted in Pursat province
(Pursat): The Anlong Reap Administrative Police Force, in cooperation with the District Police Inspectorate and the Veal Veng District Military Base, led by Colonel Theang Leng, Veal Veng District Police Inspector, raided a 2-hectare marijuana plantation site. And burn the exhibits on the spot.
The above transaction took place on July 18, 2020 at the point of O70 valley in Dey Krahorm village, Anlong Reap commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
According to the report, the cannabis cultivation site has an area of about 2 hectares due to the geographical location, rich in mountains, difficult roads, about 30 kilometers from National Road 55, so the authorities could not catch the target.
During the operation, the force burned 5,530 fresh and dried marijuana trees and a plantation hut.
