Such forms of land tenure are known in the legal sense as usufruct. We will review the definition of usufruct, the creation of usufruct, the rights and obligations of usufructuary and the termination of usufruct.
Therefore, the legal awareness program of FRESH NEWS in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, please bring up the topic of "usufruct" to present to the people, students as follows:
Usufruct refers to the right to use and enjoy immovable property owned by others. It means that a usufruct is a legal regime that gives a person called a usufructuary the right to use land for planting crops, farming or a house for sub-lease to others and to enjoy the natural rights that exist. Like crops, in addition to usufruct, civil servants can also enjoy civilian wages from renting buildings to others.
