Farmers in Angkor Borei district, Takeo province can earn tens of thousands of dollars a year from raising shrimp, Minister of Agriculture encourages to expand production
(Takeo): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and his colleagues, on the afternoon of July 18, 2020, inspected a shrimp farm in Angkor Borei commune, Angkor Borei district, Takeo province.
Mr. Prum Vat, the owner of the farm, described the original process of raising shrimp, saying that he has been raising shrimp since 2007, now there are 10 ponds on an area of 4.5 hectares, the yield is 2-3 tons / pond with 50,000 broilers. Children.
In addition to hatching, 600,000 chicks are raised per year for on-farm raising and distribution to breeders throughout Takeo, Kampong Speu and Kandal provinces. Normally, lobsters raised for 7-8 months have 10 heads per kilogram, this size costs 6-70,000 riels per kilogram.
In addition to shrimp production, Mr. Prum Vat has invested in small-scale irrigation to supply water to farmers three times a year at a cost of 250,000 riel per hectare. Including the income from pumping services and income from the lobster farm, Uncle can earn from 6-70,000 dollars per year.
Minister Veng Sakhon praised Mr. Prum Vat's efforts to achieve success now, including income, knowledge, natural shrimp farming, hatching, water supply services, all of which show that the family economy is sustainable.
Sharing knowledge and experience in raising shrimp with breeding partners is a great way to expand the shrimp farming business to grow throughout Takeo and beyond to ensure the supply of shrimp to the local market that is currently popular. .
Minister Veng Sakhon supported and encouraged the expansion of production, especially the amount of lobsters to serve the needs of farmers and please share good experiences to beginners so that they achieve the same results as Mr. Prom. Watts, too.
At the same time, this morning, Minister Veng Sakhon and his colleagues also inspected the vegetable production of farmers in Champa village, Champa commune, Prey Kabas district, Takeo province.
Mr. Kong Vong thanked Minister Veng Sakhon and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for their constant support and technical assistance to grow his business to this day.
Mr. Veng Sakhon praised the success that Mr. Kong Vong has achieved now, starting from family farming to planting in the field, facing many problems, but now there is a net factory as a place to gather vegetables to supply the market in Phnom Penh has a business for sale Agricultural inputs, etc.
Minister Veng Sakhon added that all these factors are to make vegetable production sustainable, ensure safety, economic efficiency and household income.
