Mr. San Rithy said that the signing of this Memorandum of Understanding in partnership to promote and support the goal of developing business management and accelerating the use of modern technology for all businesses in Cambodia. Many important uses of technology include reducing costs, saving time, using less human resources, but being able to work more and earn more for the company.
(Kratie): The daughter of a Prey Lang activist in Stung Treng province who died in a traffic accident in Sambo district, Kratie province, also confirmed that her father really died in a traffic accident.
Kratie Provincial Police on July 18, 2020, came out to confirm the information on Facebook, which fabricated that a Prey Lang activist was shot dead in Sambo district, Kratie province, in a traffic accident that caused his death.
Kratie Provincial Police confirmed that the victim, Sen Sothea, a Prey Lang activist in Stung Treng Province, was very drunk on the day of the incident at around 9 pm on July 16, 2020, and fell on a motorcycle and was injured. Serious and died on arrival at Sambo Health Center.
The reason why the authorities dare to conclude this is because according to the answer of Heng Sros, who before the incident drank and traveled together.
Lt. Gen. Lon Sophat told Fresh News that on July 17, 2021, at 11 o'clock, the Kratie Provincial Police received information that there was a traffic accident in Kampong Cham commune, Sambo district, Kratie province.
Upon transporting the victim to the Sambor Commune Health Center, the doctor found that the victim was dead before reaching the health center, and Heng Sros contacted the family and rented a truck to transport the body. Traditional ceremony at the family home in Orlang village, Siem Bok commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province.
At the same time, the medical team also confirmed that the victim really died in a traffic accident, not because he was shot.
Authorities cracked down on illegal timber piles at two locations for two consecutive days, confiscating nearly 10 cubic meters of timber
(Preah Vihear): The second type of wood, nearly 10 cubic meters, which was hidden by traders in two different locations in Cheb district, Preah Vihear province, was cracked down by the District Unity Command for two consecutive days.
The district governor said that on July 16, 2020, 3,127 cubic meters of timber were confiscated and stored in Chhep Lech village, Chhep Muy commune, Chhep district, Preah Vihear province. .
On July 17, 2020, the authorities cracked down on and confiscated a total of 5,3811 cubic meters of wood hidden in the forest in Po Teap village, Mlou Prey 1 commune, Chep district.
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, once again called on all people not to forget to protect themselves from Kovit 19 disease, that is, to wear a mask and be hygienic regularly because wearing a mask and With this hygienic practice, we will protect ourselves, our families and society as a whole to join the government in implementing measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
He said this on the occasion of the leadership of professional officers, doctors and local authorities, as well as the working group continued to visit and disseminate measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 on July 18, 2020 and Provided food to needy people in Stung Karch commune, Sala Krao district, Pailin province, 40 families after they were affected by the outbreak of Covid-19 disease.
