(Banteay Meanchey): The roof of the factory, the roof of the hall and the agricultural office were damaged by strong winds at 3:30 pm on July 17, 2020 in Srah Chik village, Srah Chik commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Colonel Yort Sophal, Phnom Srok District Police Inspector, said that at 3:30 pm, heavy rain accompanied by strong winds hit Srah Chik commune in Srah Chik village, causing the rice mill to open. Chan Wat Chey Udom school caused the roof to open and the district agriculture office to open the roof.
Lt. Col. Yot Sophal said that the natural disaster caused many trees to fall and the rice mill where the owner, San Hok Ly, opened 150 corrugated iron roofs, Phnom Srok District Agriculture Office lost 50 Cyprus tiles. Wat Chey Udom Chan school sheets, 1,000 dragon dragon tiles and 15 kitchens with open zinc roof.
The inspector confirmed that in the case of natural disasters, the contraction did not cause harm to people and people's homes.
Cambodia Representative to the United Nations: Cambodia is highly committed to protecting the rights of detainees
(Geneva, Switzerland): Cambodia's Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the United Nations, Mr. An Sok Khoeun, emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia is highly committed to protecting the rights of detainees.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun made this remark during his intervention at the 44th session of the UN Human Rights Council, held on July 15, 2020.
The Cambodian representative to the United Nations added that in Cambodia, long-term pre-trial detention and overcrowding in prisons were due to the large number of cases and the large number of judges, prosecutors and defense lawyers. Set. Despite the resource constraints, Cambodia has put forward a number of legal solutions and initiatives to address these challenges.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun added that among the measures taken in the past were the establishment of three regional appeals courts, an increase in funding for support for women and girls victims, and an increase in legal aid projects.
