Kampong Thom Governor Encourages Farmers to Raise More Animals to Reduce Imports
(Kampong Thom): In order to improve the well-being of the people and reduce the import of animals from abroad, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, encouraged farmers to raise more animals to reduce imports from abroad. And especially to increase household income.
Mr. Sok Lou's encouragement was made on July 17, 2020 on the occasion that he led the inspection team of Mr. Ngy Kim Pov's pig farm in Okorki village, Chreab commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Lou praised Mr. Ngy Kim Pov's farm for taking into account the well-being of the people and encouraged them to raise more pigs and chickens to supply the local market and reduce imports. Of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The provincial governor also said that on behalf of the provincial leadership, he will try to strengthen professional officers to pay attention to prevent the transport of animals, animals with no clear source, in which Kampong Thom province has a clear checkpoint in Tang district. Kok and Stong districts.
At the same time, he will strive to facilitate legal and increase production to reduce the import of animals from external sources and increase employment for the people in our country.
During the inspection, Mr. Che Yano, CP Company Representative in Kampong Thom Province, stated that the production per batch was about 4,500 units and the production period was 25 weeks per day for 175 days, with an average weight of 100 kg per unit. G.
At the same time, he also requested the head of the Royal Government to facilitate the reduction of electricity so that farmers have low production costs to reduce high costs compared to neighboring countries.
It should be noted that Kampong Thom province has 16 pig farms and 16 chicken farms.
Tbong Khmum Provincial Governor Reminds Village-Commune Authorities to Assess Back Home Before Issuing Poor Cards
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, reminded the village-commune authorities to inspect the back of the house before issuing the poor card to the people who requested it, especially to strictly prevent the rich from cheating in their locality. .
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Cheam Chansophoan and Mr. Seak Leng, Chairman of Provincial Council, holding a meeting with village chiefs, commune chiefs, deputy commune clerks in Kork Srok commune and Chong Cheach commune, Tambor district on July 17, 2020.
Minister of Justice Tells President of Phnom Penh Municipal Court and Prosecutor to Suspend Court Proceedings on Land Dispute of 163 Families in Sen Sok District Awaiting Inspection Team
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, told the President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to examine the legal possibility to suspend the court proceedings on nearly 1 hectare of land dispute of 163 families located in Factory Village. Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, to wait for the inspection team to complete the research on this dispute.
In a letter received by Fresh News on July 18, 2020, Minister Keut Rith stated that after reviewing the complaint and the relevant documents in this case, there were complications on the dispute that could not be resolved immediately. Confirmation of specific facts to the parties to the dispute as soon as possible.
It should be informed that the decision of the Minister of Justice after receiving a complaint from Chea Sarom, a representative of 163 families who asked for professional officers to inspect the disputed land area of 9,992 square meters, located in Factory Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. There are 669 state-owned lands in Tbong Khmum province, of which 461 have no title deeds yet, the provincial administration urges to expedite the registration
(Tbong Khmum): All state property, especially state land that has not been registered in the inventory, must be registered in accordance with financial procedures to avoid illegal possession or eventual loss.
He also requested the provincial / municipal-district / commune / sangkat administrative units to pay high attention to state property by preparing their inventory books for the year 2019 as soon as possible to submit to the inspection committee.
Mr. Seak Sopheak and Mr. Kun Sophea also reminded the heads of all state property use units to manage, maintain, protect and record all state assets accurately in all aspects and to complete the inventory of the base year (2019). Accurate, timely, avoid delays that may face spending restrictions in accordance with the decision of the Royal Government.
On that occasion, Mr. Kim Tithya, Director of the Department of Economy and Finance of Tbong Khmum Province, also informed that the preparation of inventory of state property is carried out in two forms: the first form is an inventory record of all state assets. It has to be done every five years, and the second form is the rising and falling of state property, which takes place once a year during the five-year period of the base year.
He said that as a result of the preparation of inventory of state property in the main year (2019) of the municipal, district, commune, sangkat and departments around the province, a total of 103 units, while land titles are state property in a total of 669 places. There are 208 land titles (plots) and 461 land titles (plots).
Mr. Kim Tithya requested all units to prepare the 2019 inventory as soon as possible to submit to the review committee as scheduled. Kampong Thom Provincial Administration Holds a Public Forum in Chey Village, Sankor Commune, Kampong Svay District to Solve People's Problems
(Kampong Thom): Kampong Thom Provincial Administration held a public forum with many people living in Chey village, Sankor commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province to solve their problems.
This public forum was attended by Mr. Bou Men, Deputy Chairman of the National Working Group for Sankor Commune, Mr. Un Bot, Governor of Kampong Svay District, Mr. Ky Savuth Tha, Deputy Governor of Kampong Svay District, Commune Chief and Village Chief, which took place on July 17. 2020.
The governor of Kampong Svay district said in the forum that the current topic is the story of Trapeang Veng and the story of the previous road that was closed, which is a cart road down to Trapeang Veng with a size of 5 hectares. And many solutions, many messages, but do not seem to match.
Mr. Un Bot continued that what he wanted was the decision of the people as the authority as the spokesperson or to go to the provincial governor, who is the provincial land manager, to decide on the allocation of state land. Brothers in the form of social concessions or other procedures.
According to the complaints of the people named Bulo and Preng Nith, on the evening of June 15, 2020, Mr. Ky Savuth Tha, Deputy Governor of Kampong Svay District, led the incitement to the destruction of private property (destruction of fences). On the backyard.
Old commune chief Chuosuon clarified that the pond land is 100 meters wide and more than 400 meters long, which is a place for livestock. In the past, the commune level decided to give this land to these two families because this pond land Farmed for many years and there are no traces of pond capacity.
Mr. Ky Savuththa replied that he acknowledged that he had indeed signed the memorandum for the first time, but please check that he did not sign the agreement.
As a result, Mr. Un Bot, Governor of Kampong Svay District, decided to open the road and put the pond into the state, based on the opinions of the people who participated and allowed the two disputed landowners to file a complaint to the Land Dispute Committee. Province.
An area once occupied by the Khmer Rouge in Kampong Cham province will become a place of great benefit to the people
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of July 18, 2020, led a working group together with officials of the Ministry of Water Resources to inspect the 3,000-meter-long dam on the border of Prey Chhor District and Cheung Prey District, Kampong Cham Province.
Samrong commune chief Saing Chhorn said that the dam is more than 3,000 meters long, can be said to be a historical site, because in this area during the Khmer Rouge occupation, people used to build this dam, and people were killed. Many also work on the dam.
However, the dam was later damaged, and it was not until Un Chanda became governor of Kampong Cham that the dam area turned into a huge benefit to Prey Chhor and Cheung Prey districts. For irrigating their crops.
Mr. Saing Chhorn, Samrong Commune Chief, on behalf of the people, took this opportunity to express his deep gratitude to all the leaders, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has always taken care of the well-being of Citizens.
On the other hand, the commune chief would like to express his happiness and gratitude to the working group of the Ministry of Water Resources as well as the Kampong Cham provincial authorities for their efforts to complete the construction of this dam quickly, make it beautiful and full of benefits. For all farmers.
It should also be noted that according to the survey of the people living in the area, it is said that the dam in this area can also become a natural tourist area, because in this area when the flood is very gentle. On either side of the road. In the past, many people in this area came to visit, enjoy fishing and playing according to their preferences during the flood season, when there were no clean roads like now.
