Senior Minister Kun Kim urges search for homeless veterans to build houses and hand over land to them
(Central): After being announced and appointed as the Vice President and Secretary General of the Veterans Association for the new term, Senior Minister Kun Kim held a meeting with representatives from the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. As well as the leaders of the Veterans Associations throughout the 25 capitals and provinces.
The meeting was held on July 17, 2020 to disseminate the direction and work plan set by the association for the new mandate, as well as to introduce some recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
During the meeting, Senior Minister Kun Kim, on behalf of the Secretary General of the Association, who was the direct executive, thanked the representatives of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, as well as all the leaders and officials of the Association. Who have worked together to solve all problems and achieve better achievements for Cambodian veterans in the past mandate.
Mr. Kun Kim also brought the words of appreciation and high appreciation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the leadership, officials and relevant authorities who have worked hard to serve the members of the Veterans.
The Senior Minister emphasized that "the achievements of the Association as well as the relevant authorities, especially the local authorities in the past mandate, have been fully appreciated and highly praised by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Association." .
In addition to expressing Samdech Techo's praise, the Senior Minister also reminded Samdech Techo Prime Minister to remind the officials of the Association and the relevant authorities to work together to solve all the problems of veterans members effectively. Higher in the new mandate.
"Along with praising the President, he also urged us to continue our efforts to achieve better achievements for the veterans. Therefore, for the new mandate, we must also continue to work together to complete this work more steadily to achieve the wishes of the President. This was further confirmed by Senior Minister Kun Kim.
The Secretary General of the Veterans Association stated that the priority of the Association in the new mandate is to try to update the members of the Association by clearly identifying so that the veterans can receive various benefits, which is a policy provided by the Royal Government of Cambodia. .
